📌 Problem Statement

You are given a binary tree.
You must place cameras on some nodes such that:

A camera placed at a node covers:

the node itself

its parent

its immediate children

🎯 Goal: Find the minimum number of cameras required to monitor the entire tree.

📘 Example
Input Tree
        0
       /
      0
       \
        0

Output
1

Explanation

Placing a camera on the middle node covers all nodes.

💡 Key Insight (VERY IMPORTANT)

Each node can be in 3 states:

State	Meaning
0	Node needs a camera
1	Node has a camera
2	Node is covered

➡ This is a post-order traversal + greedy DP

🧩 Algorithm (Step-by-Step)

Do postorder DFS

Check left & right child states

Apply rules:

If any child needs camera → install camera

If any child has camera → node is covered

Else → node needs camera

After traversal, if root needs camera → add one

⏱ Time & Space Complexity
Metric	Value
Time	O(n)
Space	O(h)
🧑‍💻 Java Code (Interview-Ready)
class TreeNode {
    int val;
    TreeNode left, right;

    TreeNode(int val) {
        this.val = val;
    }
}

public class BinaryTreeCameras {

    private static int cameras = 0;

    public static int minCameraCover(TreeNode root) {
        if (dfs(root) == 0)
            cameras++;
        return cameras;
    }

    private static int dfs(TreeNode node) {

        // Null nodes are considered covered
        if (node == null)
            return 2;

        int left = dfs(node.left);
        int right = dfs(node.right);

        // Case 1: Child needs camera
        if (left == 0 || right == 0) {
            cameras++;
            return 1;
        }

        // Case 2: Child has camera
        if (left == 1 || right == 1) {
            return 2;
        }

        // Case 3: Node needs camera
        return 0;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        TreeNode root = new TreeNode(0);
        root.left = new TreeNode(0);
        root.left.right = new TreeNode(0);

        System.out.println(minCameraCover(root));
    }
}

🔍 Line-by-Line Explanation
State Meaning
0 → needs camera
1 → has camera
2 → covered

Null Node
if (node == null) return 2;


➡ Null nodes don’t need cameras

Installing Camera
if (left == 0 || right == 0)


➡ If child is unprotected → place camera here

Root Check
if (dfs(root) == 0)
    cameras++;


➡ Root still uncovered → add camera

